    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0805" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg799"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26724: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-26T15:00:00+01:00">December 26,
                            1942—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6143. From Tittmann. 211, December 22. My 209, December 14.<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d690-f1"/> Cardinal Secretary of State informed me today that the
                    Italian Ambassador to the Holy See on December 18 gave him verbal assurances <pb
                        facs="0806" n="800" xml:id="pg800"/> that the German Headquarters Staffs
                    would also leave Rome and transfer their residence elsewhere. [Tittmann.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d690-f1" n="62" xml:id="d690-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 5984, December 18, noon, from the Minister in Switzerland, <ref
                        target="#pg796">p. 796</ref>.</p>
            </note>
